# Normalise line endings. Without this, a Windows and a macOS developer produce
# whole-file diffs of the same file and every review drowns in noise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must keep LF or they will not execute in containers or CI.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Generated — mark so GitHub collapses them in diffs and reviewers stop reading
# lockfile churn line by line.
#
# ⚠ THE PATH MUST BE THE REAL ONE, AND A WRONG PATTERN FAILS SILENTLY.
# This said `packages/contracts/generated/**` — a directory that does not exist.
# orval writes to `packages/contracts/SRC/generated/`. A .gitattributes pattern
# that matches nothing is not an error and produces no warning: the rule simply
# never applies, so ~380 KB of generated orval output was being counted by
# GitHub Linguist as hand-written TypeScript and expanded in full in every diff.
#
# Verify a pattern rather than trusting it — this is the check that caught it:
#   git check-attr linguist-generated -- packages/contracts/src/generated/model/document.ts
# `unspecified` means the rule missed; `set` means it applies.
#
# The contracts rule now matches NO tracked file, deliberately: issue #90
# untracked the generated tree (.gitignore never applied to it because the
# files were tracked before the rule landed — an ignore rule has no effect on
# already-tracked paths). The rule stays as a belt-and-braces guard: if the
# tree is ever force-added again, it renders collapsed instead of as 380 KB of
# hand-written TypeScript, and CI stage 5c fails the build on it regardless.
pnpm-lock.yaml linguist-generated=true -diff
packages/contracts/src/generated/** linguist-generated=true -diff

